{% block content %}
<article class="election-law-page">
  <p class="crumb"><a href="/communities">Communities</a> › <a href="/communities/sagamok">Sagamok Anishnawbek</a> › <a href="/communities/sagamok/accountability">Member accountability</a> › Election law counterdraft</p>

  <header class="cover">
    <p class="cover__eyebrow">Member governance work</p>
    <h1 class="cover__title">A member counterdraft for Sagamok's election law</h1>
    <p class="cover__lede">This is a complete working law built around a simple principle: election authority belongs to members. It separates election administration from Council, protects the right to vote and run, and creates a real member recall process.</p>
    <p class="law-status">Working counterdraft · Not official or enacted</p>
    <p class="cover__byline">Member-compiled and unofficial. Formal enactment would still require community consultation, legal review and the required member vote.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="law-context" aria-label="Key choices in the counterdraft">
    <div><strong>Independent administration</strong>Members select the Election Commission. Council does not appoint the election decision-makers.</div>
    <div><strong>Real recall power</strong>A petition signed by 25% of electors requires a secret recall vote. Council has no veto.</div>
    <div><strong>Open participation</strong>No residency bar, litigation bar, candidacy fee or appeal fee.</div>
    <div><strong>Member-controlled amendments</strong>No Council-only amendment route. Protected rules can change only through a member vote.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="legal-note"><strong>Legal starting point.</strong> Section 42 of the <a href="https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/F-11.65/section-42.html">First Nations Elections Act</a> sets the federal process for moving to a community election code, including a secret member vote and publication. The counterdraft is written for discussion within that framework.</div>

  <div class="law-actions">
    <a class="btn" href="/files/sagamok-election-law-member-counterdraft.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the law full screen</a>
    <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/files/sagamok-election-law-member-counterdraft.html#part11" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Go directly to member recall</a>
  </div>

  <iframe class="law-frame" src="/files/sagamok-election-law-member-counterdraft.html" title="Sagamok Leadership Selection and Accountability Law member counterdraft"></iframe>
  <p class="frame-fallback">If the embedded document does not load, <a href="/files/sagamok-election-law-member-counterdraft.html">open the full-screen version</a>.</p>
</article>
{% endblock %}
